{"description":"`eka-standard/specification/exchange.md` documents an optional validity-horizon envelope section for `validUntil`/`lastConfirmed` but never mentions `provenance`, even though `exchange.Unit` carries `Provenance` (`json:\"provenance,omitempty\"`), the artifact schema accepts the key, and the field now travels in the package.","impact":"The implementation is ahead of the specification: a second implementation reading only the spec would drop provenance on export, which is exactly the defect just fixed here. Silence in the spec is also what let the gap sit — nothing declared what the envelope was supposed to carry.","acceptanceCriteria":"- The exchange specification states the provenance envelope field, its enum, and the absence contract (absent means human), in the same shape as the validity-horizon section.\n- The standard version is bumped for the added requirement."}